DESCRIPTION

    SQLCipher is SQLite with 256-bit AES page encryption, HMAC tamper
    detection, and PBKDF2 key derivation. Cherrybean links this package
    instead of third_party/sqlite3.

BUILD (from this Cosmo worktree)

    make -j8 o//tool/net/cherrybean
    o//tool/net/cherrybean -i third_party/sqlcipher/encrypt.lua

GITHUB

    Branch cherrybean of https://github.com/dwomick/cosmopolitan
    vendors this amalgamation. SQLCipher source for upgrade.sh is
    https://github.com/dwomick/sqlcipher branch cherrybean
    (upstream https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher).

ORIGIN

    https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher  (4.18.0, SQLite 3.53.4)
    Amalgamation generated with third_party/sqlcipher/upgrade.sh
    (configure --with-tempstore=yes --disable-tcl --disable-shared
     && make sqlite3.c), after applying patches/cosmo-vfs.patch.

LICENSE

    SQLCipher: BSD-3-Clause (Zetetic LLC)
    SQLite core: Public Domain

LOCAL CHANGES

  - crypto_mbedtls.c: sqlcipher_provider using Cosmopolitan mbedtls
    (AES-256-CBC via AES-ECB, HMAC-SHA1/256/512, PBKDF2, getrandom)
  - sqlite3_cosmo.c wraps the amalgamation plus that provider
  - patches/cosmo-vfs.patch: small APE VFS hunks (pread, mmap msync,
    errno). See patches/README. Not F2FS, not include rewrite.

UPGRADING

  SQLCipher git (../sqlcipher/cherrybean) tracks upstream. Cosmo git
  vendors the amalgamation plus crypto_mbedtls.c. After either side
  moves:

    third_party/sqlcipher/upgrade.sh [path-to-sqlcipher]

  Keep cherrybean.c / lsqlite3-sqlcipher.c as thin wrappers around
  Cosmo's redbean.c and lsqlite3.c so redbean updates are a merge
  of those two Cosmo files plus the CHERRYBEAN_SQLCIPHER ifdefs.
